# sys-kernel/linux-firmware keep-list for the 'zero' board image.
#
# The file NAME is the interface: savedconfig.eclass looks for
# <CATEGORY>/<PF>, then <CATEGORY>/<P>, then <CATEGORY>/<PN> under
# ${PORTAGE_CONFIGROOT}/etc/portage/savedconfig/ -- which in a cross emerge is
# the arm64 sysroot, not the host. 'xarm setup'/'xarm tune' copy this tree in
# VERBATIM for exactly that reason (every other fragment class gets an
# xprofile- prefix, which this lookup would never find).
#
# Everything not listed here is dropped: default USE installs 2.0 GB of
# firmware, which is more than the entire zero image. Each line is matched as
# a substring against the File:/Link: entries of upstream's WHENCE, so listing
# the real file is enough -- the compat symlink at the top of /lib/firmware is
# pulled in with it and its target appended to the list automatically
# (${FILESDIR}/linux-firmware-copy-firmware-r9.patch, which is what puts
# --firmware-list back into upstream's copy-firmware.sh; upstream itself
# dropped that option, so this only works with Gentoo's patched ebuild).
#
# COMFAST CF-922AC == MediaTek MT7612U, driven by the in-tree mt76x2u module
# that sys-kernel/raspberrypi-image already ships. modinfo asks for the
# UNPREFIXED names (mt7662.bin, mt7662_rom_patch.bin); WHENCE ships the blobs
# under mediatek/ plus a Link: for each, so both ends of that pair have to
# survive the trim. ~108 KB in total.
mediatek/mt7662.bin
mediatek/mt7662_rom_patch.bin
